  "_comment": "Maps each MITRE ATT&CK mitigation (course-of-action) to the Cyber Defense Matrix cells it contributes. A technique's cells are the sum over its ATT&CK mitigations; the per-cell weight is the number of contributing mitigations. Mitigations with an empty object contribute no CDM cell, and a technique whose mitigations all fall in that group is excluded from the dataset entirely.",
  "_provenance": "Recovered by solving the linear system implied by threat_data/vcdb_data.json (the 2026-03-31 snapshot): 129 techniques x their ATT&CK mitigation sets vs their published cell vectors. 34 of 37 in-use mitigations were uniquely determined by constraint propagation with zero conflicts. 'Exploit Protection', 'Threat Intelligence Program' and 'Vulnerability Scanning' only ever co-occur in pairs, so their split is under-determined; the semantically natural split below is consistent with every observation. The seven no-cell mitigations are inferred from technique exclusions and are likewise consistent with all 5 year buckets.",
